From a4c02e63d8da0ecc92381b69cfd859406b5694e8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: arshiyaazim <arshiya.azim.1980@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 13:24:39 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] fix(vessel): one logical order per business identity
 across fragments

Repeated order fragments for the same Lighter, Master Mobile and shift on the
same day were each parsed into their own Draft, so the later Admin Confirmation
matched 2-3 candidates and was refused as ASSIGNMENT_MATCH_AMBIGUOUS.

- vessel-match: add orderIdentity/orderBusinessDay and collapse candidates by
  logical business identity before the ambiguity test. The earliest fragment
  represents the order, so the original Order Message ID is preserved.
- escort-register: record a deterministic logicalOrderId on each Draft. No row
  and no source message is dropped or overwritten; the archive stays the
  evidence of record.
- Genuine competition (different Lighter, Master, shift or day) still fails
  closed as AMBIGUOUS. Verified-Admin, same-chat and chronology rules unchanged.
- Tests: real November 3 fixtures (Rahman Asif, Fardin-7, Borkot Jidan), the
  November 2 control, distinct duties, forwarded copies and replay idempotency.
